side yet. A close above $366.22 would put it back in an uptrend and support the upside; a close below $289.77 would break the year's floor and support the downside. The chart disagrees with management for now: they describe demand above supply, while price sits under its long-term average and 30% under its 52-week high.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Dec 9 report:</strong> whether the fiscal 2027 AI figure of about $115B is confirmed in writing, and the new size of the financing backstop.</li><li><strong>The 10-K:</strong> how much customer debt Broadcom now guarantees, and for whom.</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> a close above $366.22 or below $289.77.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: release and 10-Q figures, the CFO change (8-K) and governance facts (2026 proxy, read in part). Thin: call detail and the fiscal 2027 and 2028 AI figures (one automated transcript); the $92B financing figure (press report, no filing cited); the Dec 9 date (Webull only).</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://investors.broadcom.com/news-releases/news-release-details/broadcom-inc-announces-third-quarter-fiscal-year-2026-financial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FQ3 release</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.webull.com/news/15511095937917952\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call transcript</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001730168/000173016826000051/avgo-05032026x8kxex99.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FQ2 release (prior guide)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001730168/000173016826000080/avgo-20260802.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-Q</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.boardroomalpha.com/sec/avgo-def-14a-2026-03-02-0001193125-26-085691\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2026 proxy statement (Boardroom Alpha copy)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.boardroomalpha.com/sec/avgo-8-k-2026-04-